  "term": "IRM",
  "definition": "IRM stands for Inclusive Research Methods, an approach to planning and conducting research so it is representative, accessible, and relevant to a wide range of people, including under-served groups. In this source, it is part of a broader strategy that uses co-production and practical methods to build inclusivity across the research process.",
